WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.109 --> 00:00:06.109
The minions, those banana-loving, dungaree-wearing,
yellow mini-sidekicks from the Despicable

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:12.169
Me movies are back causing mirth and mayhem,
but this time they've got their very own movie!

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:16.940
But can Gru's loveable lackeys actually sustain
their own 90-minute feature?

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.570
Well, first of all, what's not to love about
the minions?

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:26.520
They're fun and funny, adorable little mischief-makers
with an irrepressible, child-like spirit.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.950
Secondly, things do kick off well with the
fast-paced film opening at the dawn of time

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:36.210
and the birth of the minions' and then whisking
us through their chequered history as the

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.870
flunkies of various villains throughout the
ages.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:44.210
After globetrotting through the centuries,
the movie settles down in the late 1960s,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:48.770
which means you can expect plenty of pop culture
references and a fantastic soundtrack stuffed

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:53.050
full of classic tracks including The Doors,
The Stones and The Beatles.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:57.640
And the Minions themselves get some superb
song-and-dance numbers – and my favourite

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.420
of those is from an absolutely timeless Hollywood
musical.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.970
Speaking of which, do stay to the very end
of the credits; otherwise you'll miss a revolutionary

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.950
routine from the stars of the movie!

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.580
As you'd expect if you've seen either of the
Despicable Me movies, this spin-off prequel

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:18.821
is filled with the minions' trademark babble,
which manages to be both no language and every

00:01:18.821 --> 00:01:21.520
language all at once, and provides a good
deal of humour.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.190
And, of course, their lack of conventional
speech means there's also loads of entertaining

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:30.080
slapstick comedy, including a particularly
amusing game of football.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.710
All of which means there's more than enough
to keep children entertained, and there's

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.330
enough for adults here too.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:40.100
London, where much of the movie's main action
takes place, gets typical movie treatment,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:45.240
with lots of tea-drinking, rain, red telephone
boxes, cobbled streets, bowler hats, Big Ben,

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.650
the Tube, and so on, but like so much else
in the movie it's beautifully animated in

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:50.870
its details.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:56.229
But where Minions does fall down, certainly
compared with Despicable Me, is in the central

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:57.400
villain department.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.580
Although Sandra Bullock does a good job with
the material she's given as female supervillain

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:07.380
Scarlett Overkill, her character as it's written
just doesn't live up to its potential.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.651
Basically, Scarlett's built up as the most
amazing villain ever and yet, although she

00:02:11.651 --> 00:02:16.370
does get to kick a bit of ass and we do see
the stacks of loot she's amassed from the

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:21.970
many heists we're told she's pulled off, we
never actually see her commit any crazy crimes.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:27.120
And, I'm not quite sure why Scarlett would
actually need the minions as she's got all

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.770
the high-tech gadgetry designed for her by
her scientist husband, who's played by Mad

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:32.770
Men's Jon Hamm.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:36.430
But I guess the simple answer is that this
is the minions' movie!

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:41.930
So, to sum up: Minions is full of zany action,
cute 'n' crazy central characters, and fizzing

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.930
with energy, despite having a lacklustre big
baddie.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:49.260
At 90 minutes, it's an enjoyable romp through
the history of what must be the best-known

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.390
yellow cartoon characters since The Simpsons.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.140
Minions gets 3 and a half out of 5 Flicks.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.320
Now, what do you think of Minions?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.790
And how do you think it compares to the Despicable
Me movies?

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.780
And what would you like to see happen in a
Minions or Despicable Me sequel?

